{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe 884-unit hardening oracle invokes production `_convert` once per unit. `_convert` currently resolves `reconciler.dc_pandoc_timeout_s` on every invocation. A runtime trace on current origin/main d05bf2bc1be observed 100 Pandoc plus 102 `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` subprocesses for 100 conversions; resolving once at the render-pass boundary preserved identical outputs and reduced the trace to 100 Pandoc plus 3 one-time root probes. The prior 884-unit trace observed 1,770 total Popen calls (884 Pandoc + 886 root discovery). This is separate from the copied legacy oracle removed by absolute-diplomatic-snowyowl.\n\n## Contract and prior disposition\n- Preserve all real Pandoc calls, corpus units, byte expectations, timeout configurability, per-unit fallback, timeout, and process-group reap behavior.\n- absolute-diplomatic-snowyowl approved immutable outputs only for the copied legacy side and retained all 884 real production conversions. harmless-wavy-osprey approved session-scoped sharing that reduced duplicate work, while coercive-paediatric-bug rejected parallelism that does not reduce aggregate runner usage. No tracker ticket rejects render-pass configuration injection.\n- Full replacement of product Pandoc calls remains out of scope because ADR 0095 requires the real pinned boundary in every conversion assertion.\n\n## OSS consensus research (2026-08-14)\nAll three surveyed projects are active, unarchived, and popular: Django (88,426 stars; pushed 2026-08-13) lazily resolves each setting and caches it in `LazySettings.__dict__`; Black (41,804 stars; pushed 2026-08-10) reads pyproject configuration at CLI setup and passes resolved `mode` into multi-file workers; pytest (14,416 stars; pushed 2026-08-12) exposes its resolved Config as a session-scoped `pytestconfig` fixture. Consensus is 3/3 for resolving loop/session invariants once and passing them to repeated work.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add a held-out behavioral oracle with three proven renderable units and assert exactly one `_pandoc_timeout()` resolution for the whole render pass.\n2. Resolve timeout once in `render_markdown_to_wiki`; pass it through `_render_unit` and `_convert` using optional parameters so direct two-argument callers retain safe default behavior. The direct `_render_unit` caller at test_wiki_render_corpus.py:325 remains valid.\n3. Update the two `_convert` monkeypatch stand-ins at test_wiki_render.py:268/278 to accept the optional argument supplied by the public render path.\n4. In the 884-unit direct hardening loop, resolve timeout once outside the loop and pass it to `_convert`; keep exact expected bytes and all 884 real Pandoc invocations.\n5. Run held-out RED -> fixer -> GREEN, defect-seeded RED, focused hardening/corpus tests, lint, typecheck, and paired subprocess/timing measurement. The fresh-process measurement must observe 884 Pandoc launches, exactly one timeout resolution, and at most 3 one-time Git-root probes.\n6. Push through Gerrit; merge only after LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, no unresolved comments, then record CI and runner savings. Back-out is a Gerrit revert restoring per-call timeout resolution.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A render pass with three renderable units calls `_pandoc_timeout()` exactly once.\n- [ ] The hardening oracle launches all 884 real production Pandoc conversions.\n- [ ] A fresh 884-unit trace launches at most 3 `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` probes.\n- [ ] Non-default timeout configuration remains observable between separate render passes.\n- [ ] Per-unit timeout fallback behavior remains covered.\n- [ ] Pandoc stdin and argv behavior remains covered.\n- [ ] Byte-equivalence to all 884 immutable expected outputs remains covered.\n- [ ] Whole-process-group reap behavior remains covered.\n- [ ] Held-out RED/GREEN and exact defect-seeded RED are recorded.\n- [ ] Before/after subprocess counts and wall time quantify savings without claiming more than the evidence.\n- [ ] Focused tests, lint, and typecheck pass.\n- [ ] LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 pass before merge.\n- [ ] Final report cites OSS sources and prior-ticket dispositions."}},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786701386301140001,"uuid":"2523b73a-e66c-465b-a890-45a36608ac88"}